# oracle: point dipoles rotating under fix nve/sphere update dipole (dynamics of pair lj/cut/dipole/long 2.5 with kspace_style pppm/dipole 1.0e-4 and kspace_modify gewald 0.5 mesh 12 12 12 order 5), 108 fcc dipoles, 40 steps of 0.002: pe, elong, press and the dipole positions after the run
# oracle-files: w135pd_md_sphere_mu.dump
# measured with native LAMMPS (/home/roy/.local/bin/lmp, b332f28), engine vs native fixture after 40 steps: max relative error 1.2e-14 (thermo), 1.3e-12 (forces and positions), 2.9e-15 (dipole moments); under Node 24. Re-measured under Node 20: below 1e-8.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      hybrid sphere dipole
boundary        p p p
lattice         fcc 0.4
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
set             group all diameter 1.0
set             group all density 1.0
set             group all dipole/random 4421 0.7
pair_style      lj/cut/dipole/long 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0
kspace_style    pppm/dipole 1.0e-4
kspace_modify   gewald 0.5 mesh 12 12 12 order 5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0
velocity        all create 0.5 4928 mom yes rot yes dist gaussian
fix             1 all nve/sphere update dipole
timestep        0.002
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl ecoul elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          10
run             40
write_dump      all custom w135pd_md_sphere_mu.dump id mux muy muz modify format float %.15g sort id
